ves the need for component factory  resolver being injected into the  constructor  iv creates the opportunity to  instantiate the component with view  container ref dot create component  without creating an associated factory  followed by that we have the  modifications in the angular package  format the angular package format apf  has been streamlined and modernized to  better serve developers to streamline  the apf10 version 13 the team removed  older output formats including view  engine specific metadata to modernize it  they have standardized on more modern  javascript formats such as es2020  libraries built with the latest version  of the apf will no longer require the  use of ngcc as a result of these changes  library developers can expect leaner  package outputs and faster execution  now the fourth update bye bye to  internet explorer 11. removing ie 11  support allows angular to leverage  modern browser features such as css  variables and web animations via native  web apis what's more the apps will be  smaller and load faster because we can  remove ie specific polyfills and code  paths  it also removes the need for  differential loading developers will  benefit from improved apis and well  infrastructure while application users  will benefit from faster loading and an  improved user experience  now the fifth update  framework modifications and dependency  updates  angular version 13 also features some  helpful updates and important changes  first up rxjs 7.4 is the default for  apps created with ng new existing apps  using rxjs version 6 will have to  manually update using the npm install  rxjs at 7.4 command  now let's look at the sixth update  improve testing and debugging  there are important improvements to  testbet that now do a better job of  tearing down test modules and  environments after each test the dom is  now cleaned after every test and  developers can expect faster less memory  intensive less independent and more  optimized tests  now let's jump into the seventh update  that is the performance improvements  these recent updates in angular 13 have  undoubtedly resulted in major  improvements by introducing unusual  modifications such as the opt-in feature  is enabled by default global scripts and  bundles have been optimized in union  type templates auto completion is  supported  now let's look at the final update that  is improvements in the angular command  line interface  angular now supports the use of  persistent build cache by default for  new version 13 projects the valuable  feedback from rfc persistent built cache  by default led to this tooling update  that results in up to 68 improvement in  build speed and more ergonomic options  and so with that we have come to an end  of this short video on angular 13. i  hope this video helped you if you have  any questions let us know in the  comments thank you so much for being  here and watch out for more videos from  simply learn  hi there if you like this video  subscribe to the simply learn youtube  channel and click here to watch similar  videos turn it up and get certified  click here
 

